at aren't suitable for you or maybe  you're going to be finding properties  that you can't quite afford to buy  so what are you going to do with them  flush them down the toilet no  you're going to pass them on to an  investor and charge a fee and use that  fee to put towards your next property  investment yourself  so what is bespoke deal sourcing  one of the problems to do for deal  sources is that they'll go out there  they'll spend weeks finding a deal  they'll negotiate the deal they'll have  the offer accepted  yes but then they can't find an investor  to sell the deal to and and all their  investors are going to be  wasting time messing around so what's  the way to stop that happening  and i always teach this i say to my to  my  students on samuel 365 i say before you  find a deal find an investor  because if you find some investors and  you say what are you looking for what  kind of a  deal are you looking for they'll tell  you what they're looking for and then  you go out and find that deal for them  that's the way to do it now one of the  problems with that is people will tell  you all day long  yes i'd love to buy you know a big  mansion in london and i've got all the  money  and then you go and find it and then  they go oh actually now's not the right  time  and it's like okay oh i'd like to buy 10  hmos in manchester  you know i've got loads of money and  then you'll run around finding the deals  and you'll go to the investor and you'll  say i found a hm in manchester though  well let me just speak to my wife and  let me just do  and the time wasters so what are you  going to do to solve that problem  well you can ask them for their proof of  funds  and their photo id before you start  finding deals  of course you can make sure say to them  are you actually ready to buy great  but what i would recommend doing is  something called bespoke  deal sourcing here's how it works you  say to an investor  mr investor what are you looking to buy  and they'll say 